Written `ADR-001-notification-architecture.md`. The recommendation is **Redis Streams** — the deciding factors are:

- **No new infrastructure** (Redis already in production), which maps to the 6-person team with no Kafka experience and no dedicated infra engineer.
- **2-week time-to-value** (streams integrate into the Flask monolith in days; Kafka would consume the entire window on setup alone).
- **Throughput ceiling is irrelevant** — even at 10x growth (5k msg/s), Redis handles orders of magnitude more; Kafka's millions-per-second capacity is wasted here.
- **Exactly-once via idempotency** — consumer groups give at-least-once; PostgreSQL unique constraints give deduplication for billing notifications. Simpler and equally reliable at our scale vs. Kafka's transactional EOS.
- **Budget** — zero marginal cost vs. hundreds/month for managed Kafka.

The ADR also documents the trade-offs honestly: memory-bound retention, single-node availability (mitigated by Sentinel), and the scaling ceiling well beyond our 10x horizon.
